## 4. API Architecture

### 4.1 Microservices Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph Mobile Apps
        CA[Company App]
        AA[Admin App]
        TA[Technician App]
    end
    
    subgraph API Gateway
        AG[API Gateway / Load Balancer]
    end
    
    subgraph Services
        AS[Auth Service]
        RS[Request Service]
        TS[Master Team Service]
        JS[Job Service]
        ATS[Attendance Service]
        SBS[Substitute Service]
        SLS[Salary Service]
        NS[Notification Service]
        BS[Billing Service]
        MS[Media Service]
        LS[Location Service]
    end
    
    subgraph External
        FCM[Firebase Cloud Messaging]
        GMP[Google Maps API]
        SG[SendGrid / Email]
        S3[Cloud Storage]
    end
    
    subgraph Database
        PG[(PostgreSQL)]
        RD[(Redis Cache)]
    end
    
    CA --> AG
    AA --> AG
    TA --> AG
    
    AG --> AS
    AG --> RS
    AG --> TS
    AG --> JS
    AG --> ATS
    AG --> SBS
    AG --> SLS
    AG --> NS
    AG --> BS
    AG --> MS
    AG --> LS
    
    NS --> FCM
    LS --> GMP
    BS --> SG
    MS --> S3
    
    AS --> PG
    RS --> PG
    TS --> PG
    JS --> PG
    ATS --> PG
    SBS --> PG
    SLS --> PG
    BS --> PG
    
    AS --> RD
    JS --> RD
    ATS --> RD
```

### 4.2 Core API Endpoints

#### Authentication Service
```
POST   /api/auth/register          - Register new user (any role)
POST   /api/auth/login             - User login
POST   /api/auth/refresh           - Refresh JWT token
POST   /api/auth/forgot-password   - Password reset
```

#### Request Service (Company App)
```
POST   /api/requests               - Create service request
GET    /api/requests               - List company's requests
GET    /api/requests/:id           - Get request details
PUT    /api/requests/:id           - Update request
GET    /api/requests/:id/status    - Get current status
```

#### Team Service (Admin App)
```
GET    /api/technicians            - List all technicians
GET    /api/technicians/available  - Get available technicians
GET    /api/technicians/skills     - Filter by skills
POST   /api/jobs/:id/lead          - Assign team lead (confidential)
```

#### Master Team Service
```
POST   /api/jobs/:id/master-team              - Create master team for job
GET    /api/jobs/:id/master-team              - Get master team details
POST   /api/master-teams/:id/members          - Add technician to master team
DELETE /api/master-teams/:id/members/:techId  - Remove from master team
PUT    /api/master-teams/:id/members/:techId  - Update member status
GET    /api/master-teams/:id/members          - List all master team members
```

#### Daily Assignment Service
```
POST   /api/jobs/:id/daily-assignments        - Create daily assignment
GET    /api/jobs/:id/daily-assignments        - List all daily assignments
GET    /api/daily-assignments/:id             - Get assignment details
PUT    /api/daily-assignments/:id             - Update assignment
GET    /api/daily-assignments/:id/technicians - Get assigned technicians for day
POST   /api/daily-assignments/:id/select      - Select technicians for the day
```

#### Attendance Service
```
POST   /api/attendance/check-in               - Technician check-in
POST   /api/attendance/check-out              - Technician check-out
GET    /api/attendance/daily/:assignmentId    - Get daily attendance records
GET    /api/attendance/technician/:techId     - Get technician's attendance history
PUT    /api/attendance/:id                    - Update attendance record
GET    /api/attendance/job/:jobId/summary     - Get attendance summary for job
```

#### Substitute Service
```
POST   /api/substitutes                       - Request substitute
GET    /api/substitutes/pending               - List pending substitute requests
GET    /api/substitutes/:id                   - Get substitute request details
PUT    /api/substitutes/:id/approve           - Approve substitute request
PUT    /api/substitutes/:id/reject            - Reject substitute request
PUT    /api/substitutes/:id/salary-confirm    - Confirm salary deduction
GET    /api/substitutes/job/:jobId            - List all substitutes for job
```

#### Salary Service
```
GET    /api/salary/job/:jobId/calculate       - Calculate salaries for job
GET    /api/salary/technician/:techId         - Get technician salary details
POST   /api/salary/job/:jobId/process         - Process salary payments
GET    /api/salary/job/:jobId/summary         - Get salary summary report
PUT    /api/salary/:id/adjust                 - Adjust salary record
GET    /api/salary/reports/monthly            - Generate monthly salary report
```

#### Job Service
```
GET    /api/jobs                   - List jobs (role-based)
GET    /api/jobs/:id               - Get job details
PUT    /api/jobs/:id/status        - Update job status
POST   /api/jobs/:id/evidence      - Upload work evidence
GET    /api/jobs/:id/location      - Get location details
```

#### Technician Response
```
GET    /api/invitations            - Get pending invitations
PUT    /api/invitations/:id        - Respond to invitation
GET    /api/my-jobs                - Get assigned jobs
GET    /api/my-attendance          - Get my attendance records
POST   /api/availability           - Set availability for dates
```

#### Signature & Completion
```
POST   /api/jobs/:id/signature     - Upload supervisor signature
GET    /api/jobs/:id/signature     - Get signature (admin only)
```

#### Billing Service
```
POST   /api/jobs/:id/invoice       - Generate invoice
GET    /api/invoices               - List invoices
POST   /api/invoices/:id/send      - Send invoice via email
GET    /api/invoices/:id/pdf       - Download invoice PDF
---

## 4.3 Urban Company-Style Enhancements

> [!TIP]
> These patterns are inspired by **Urban Company's successful architecture** and adapted for MaintainU's B2B industrial maintenance context.

---

### 4.3.1 Service Status State Machine

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> REQUESTED: Company submits request
    
    REQUESTED --> REVIEWING: Admin views request
    REVIEWING --> TEAM_FORMING: Admin starts team selection
    
    TEAM_FORMING --> INVITATIONS_SENT: Invites sent to technicians
    INVITATIONS_SENT --> TEAM_CONFIRMED: Enough acceptances
    INVITATIONS_SENT --> TEAM_FORMING: Need replacements
    
    TEAM_CONFIRMED --> DISPATCHED: Location & details sent
    
    DISPATCHED --> ON_THE_WAY: Technicians en route
    ON_THE_WAY --> ARRIVED: Team reaches site
    
    ARRIVED --> WORK_STARTED: Check-in confirmed
    WORK_STARTED --> IN_PROGRESS: Work ongoing
    IN_PROGRESS --> IN_PROGRESS: Status updates
    
    IN_PROGRESS --> WORK_COMPLETED: Work finished
    WORK_COMPLETED --> SIGNATURE_PENDING: Awaiting sign-off
    
    SIGNATURE_PENDING --> COMPLETED: Supervisor signed
    COMPLETED --> INVOICED: Invoice generated
    INVOICED --> PAID: Payment received
    
    PAID --> [*]
    
    REQUESTED --> CANCELLED: Company/Admin cancels
    TEAM_FORMING --> CANCELLED: Cannot form team
    CANCELLED --> [*]
```

### Status Codes Reference

| Status | Code | Description | Visible To |
|--------|------|-------------|------------|
| Requested | `REQUESTED` | New request submitted | Company, Admin |
| Reviewing | `REVIEWING` | Admin is processing | Company, Admin |
| Team Forming | `TEAM_FORMING` | Selecting technicians | Admin |
| Invitations Sent | `INVITES_SENT` | Awaiting responses | Admin, Technicians |
| Team Confirmed | `TEAM_CONFIRMED` | Team finalized | Company, Admin |
| Dispatched | `DISPATCHED` | Team has location details | All |
| On The Way | `ON_THE_WAY` | Team traveling to site | Company, Admin |
| Arrived | `ARRIVED` | Team at location | Company, Admin |
| Work Started | `WORK_STARTED` | Check-in complete | All |
| In Progress | `IN_PROGRESS` | Work ongoing | All |
| Work Completed | `WORK_COMPLETED` | Work finished | All |
| Signature Pending | `SIGN_PENDING` | Awaiting supervisor signature | Company, Admin |
| Completed | `COMPLETED` | Job done, signature received | All |
| Invoiced | `INVOICED` | Invoice sent | Company, Admin |
| Paid | `PAID` | Payment received | Company, Admin |
| Cancelled | `CANCELLED` | Job cancelled | All |

---

### 4.3.2 Escrow Payment Architecture

> [!IMPORTANT]
> MaintainU uses an **escrow-like payment model** to protect both companies and technicians.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Company
    participant App as MaintainU App
    participant PG as Payment Gateway
    participant ESC as Escrow Account
    participant A as Admin
    participant T as Technician Wallet
    
    Note over C,T: Payment Flow
    
    C->>App: Receives Invoice
    C->>PG: Initiates Payment (UPI/Card/NetBanking)
    
    PG->>PG: INITIATED
    PG->>PG: AUTHORIZED
    PG->>ESC: CAPTURED → Funds held
    
    Note over ESC: Money held in escrow until work verified
    
    A->>A: Verifies work completion
    A->>A: Confirms no disputes
    
    ESC->>ESC: SETTLEMENT TRIGGERED
    ESC->>A: Platform Commission (X%)
    ESC->>T: Technician Payment (100% - Commission)
    
    A->>T: Push: Payment credited ₹XX,XXX
    
    Note over C,T: If Dispute
    
    alt Dispute Raised
        C->>A: Raises dispute
        A->>A: Investigation
        ESC->>ESC: HOLD - Payment paused
        A->>A: Resolution
        alt Refund
            ESC->>C: Partial/Full refund
        else Release
            ESC->>T: Payment released
        end
    end
```

### Payment States

```
INITIATED → AUTHORIZED → CAPTURED → HELD → SETTLED
                                      ↓
                                  DISPUTED → REFUNDED / RELEASED
```

### Payment Database Schema Addition

```mermaid
erDiagram
    PAYMENT {
        uuid id PK
        uuid invoice_id FK
        uuid company_id FK
        float amount
        string currency
        string payment_method
        string gateway_txn_id
        string status
        float platform_fee
        float technician_payout
        timestamp initiated_at
        timestamp captured_at
        timestamp settled_at
    }
    
    PAYOUT {
        uuid id PK
        uuid job_id FK
        uuid technician_id FK
        float amount
        string status
        string bank_reference
        timestamp processed_at
    }
    
    DISPUTE {
        uuid id PK
        uuid payment_id FK
        uuid raised_by FK
        string reason
        string description
        string status
        string resolution
        timestamp raised_at
        timestamp resolved_at
    }
```

---

### 4.3.3 Real-Time GPS Tracking

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph TechApp["📱 Technician App"]
        GPS[GPS Module]
        LOC[Location Service]
    end
    
    subgraph Backend["☁️ Backend"]
        WS[WebSocket Server]
        REDIS[(Redis Pub/Sub)]
        TRACK[Tracking Service]
    end
    
    subgraph Consumers["👀 Viewers"]
        CA[Company App]
        AA[Admin Dashboard]
        MAP[Live Map View]
    end
    
    GPS -->|Every 30s| LOC
    LOC -->|Coordinates| WS
    WS -->|Publish| REDIS
    REDIS -->|Subscribe| TRACK
    TRACK -->|Broadcast| CA
    TRACK -->|Broadcast| AA
    AA --> MAP
```

### Tracking Data Points

| Field | Value | Purpose |
|-------|-------|---------|
| `technician_id` | UUID | Who is being tracked |
| `job_id` | UUID | Which job they're on |
| `latitude` | Float | Current lat |
| `longitude` | Float | Current long |
| `accuracy` | Float | GPS accuracy in meters |
| `speed` | Float | Movement speed |
| `heading` | Float | Direction of travel |
| `battery` | Int | Device battery % |
| `timestamp` | DateTime | When captured |
| `status` | String | ON_WAY / ARRIVED / WORKING |

### Tracking API Endpoints

```
POST   /api/tracking/update           - Send location update (Technician)
GET    /api/tracking/job/:jobId       - Get all technician locations for job
GET    /api/tracking/technician/:id   - Get technician's current location
WS     /ws/tracking/:jobId            - WebSocket for real-time updates
```

### ETA Calculation

```
ETA = Google Maps Distance API (current location → job location)
     + Buffer time (traffic, weather adjustments)
     + Historical data (technician's average travel time)
```

