### 4.3.4 Rating & Feedback System

> [!NOTE]
> Ratings directly affect future job allocation, creating accountability and quality assurance.

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph Collection["📝 Feedback Collection"]
        C1[Company rates Technicians]
        C2[Company rates Overall Service]
        C3[Optional detailed review]
    end
    
    subgraph Storage["💾 Data Storage"]
        R1[Individual technician ratings]
        R2[Service quality scores]
        R3[Review text + tags]
    end
    
    subgraph Impact["📊 Impact"]
        I1[Future job allocation priority]
        I2[Technician incentive eligibility]
        I3[Quality alerts for Admin]
        I4[Platform trust score]
    end
    
    Collection --> Storage --> Impact
```

### Rating Flow (After Job Completion)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Company User
    participant App as Company App
    participant API as Backend
    participant T as Technician Profile
    
    Note over C,T: 24 hours after job completion
    
    App->>C: Push: "Rate your recent service"
    C->>App: Opens rating screen
    
    App->>C: Overall Experience (1-5 stars)
    App->>C: Rate Team Lead (1-5 stars)
    App->>C: Rate Team (1-5 stars)
    App->>C: Tags: Punctual, Professional, Skilled, Clean
    App->>C: Optional written review
    
    C->>API: Submit ratings
    API->>T: Update technician avg rating
    API->>API: Update allocation priority
    
    alt Low Rating (< 3)
        API->>Admin: Alert: Low rating received
        Admin->>Admin: Review case
    end
```

### Rating Database Schema

```mermaid
erDiagram
    RATING {
        uuid id PK
        uuid job_id FK
        uuid company_id FK
        uuid technician_id FK
        int overall_score
        int punctuality
        int professionalism
        int skill_quality
        int cleanliness
        json tags
        string review_text
        timestamp created_at
    }
    
    TECHNICIAN_SCORE {
        uuid technician_id PK
        float avg_rating
        int total_jobs
        int total_ratings
        float punctuality_avg
        float skill_avg
        int five_star_count
        int low_rating_count
        timestamp last_updated
    }
```

### Allocation Priority Formula

```
Priority Score = (Avg Rating × 0.4) 
               + (Jobs Completed × 0.2) 
               + (Acceptance Rate × 0.2) 
               + (Recency × 0.1) 
               + (Distance × 0.1)

Higher score = Higher priority in team suggestions
```

---

### 4.3.5 Smart Dispatch Engine (Admin Assisted)

> [!NOTE]
> Unlike Urban Company's fully automated dispatch, MaintainU uses **admin-assisted smart suggestions** because B2B industrial jobs often require human judgment.

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph Input["📥 Request Input"]
        R1[Service Type]
        R2[Location]
        R3[Date/Time]
        R4[Skill Requirements]
    end
    
    subgraph Engine["🧠 Dispatch Engine"]
        F1[Filter by Skills]
        F2[Filter by Location/Distance]
        F3[Check Availability]
        F4[Sort by Rating]
        F5[Sort by Acceptance History]
        F6[Generate Ranked List]
    end
    
    subgraph Output["📤 Admin Recommendations"]
        O1[Top 10 Recommended Technicians]
        O2[Match Score per Technician]
        O3[Reason for Recommendation]
    end
    
    Input --> Engine --> Output
    
    Admin[Admin Reviews] --> O1
    Admin --> FinalSelection[Final Selection]
```

### Recommendation API

```
GET /api/dispatch/recommendations
Query params:
  - job_id: UUID
  - service_type: string
  - location: lat,long
  - date: date
  - team_size: int

Response:
{
  recommendations: [
    {
      technician_id: "uuid",
      name: "John Smith",
      match_score: 92,
      distance_km: 5.2,
      rating: 4.8,
      availability: "AVAILABLE",
      skills_match: ["Electrical", "Industrial"],
      recent_jobs: 15,
      recommendation_reasons: [
        "Top rated in Electrical",
        "5km from location",
        "95% acceptance rate"
      ]
    },
    ...
  ]
}
```

